      "writtenOn": "2021-07-12T14:57:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This passes the same socket file descriptor to (potentially) multiple processes. What does that actually do? What happens if several processes try to read from it at the same time?",
      "revId": "732c3b4963538ec7fe54f44c420984d50be42612",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "710183d9_1a0bbcff",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-12T16:17:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I haven\u0027t tried by myself, but in theory, they will compete with each other to read from the same socket. So each of them will probably get only fragments of the stream.\n\nI don\u0027t think this is a big issue as VMs are expected to be owned by a single app, not shared by multiple processes. I\u0027ve updated the java side document to clarify this behavior.",
      "parentUuid": "06b41be5_c7228f7e",
